Janis Papanagnou wrote:
> Doug Freyburger wrote:
>> 
>> Regular A's have a 5% chance of trying to make their rustproof long
>> sword into Sunsword or Demonbane. Archons have a 100% chance of trying
>> to make their rustproof long sword into Sunsword or Demonbane (usual
>> stuff about the odds when one not the other already exists etc here). 
>> Because it was not rustproof it did not come from that source.  You
>> probably found Sunsword on the floor likely in a shop.  It's possible it
>> came from a death drop not an initial inventory.
>
> BTW, I didn't knew that angels can convert a sword, I always thought it
> would come from their initial equipment.

Semantics - The initial equipment code gives A's a rustproof long sword.
For a regular A there's a 1-in-20 chance the code tries to convert it to
an artifact.  For an archon there's a 1-in-1 chance the code tries to
convert it to an artifact.  If it tries to convert to an artifact then
it does a 50-50 chance of Demonbane or Sunsword.  If the chosen artifact
does not yet exist then that monster gets that artifact.  It's not a
choice by the monster it's the choices the code makes when the monster
is created.  At points the chances can come out with archons having a
50-50 chance of getting the one that does not yet exist otherwise a
rustproof non-artifact +1 or better long sword.

It's what I mean in my (usual stuff about the odds ...) comment.

I usually like to collect artifacts.  I kill plenty of hostiles so I
generally have the numerical alignment (piety) to spare to kill
peacefuls.  A's tend to have those two artifacts so until I have them
both I take out A's at my convenience if I'm in good health and there is
no other visible danger.

There's an added benefit thrown in among my comments above - The long
swords in the inventories of A's are rustproof and at least +1
enchanted.  Not bad if you have seen few long swords yet in the game.


